{"availability":"available","full":"nilaymaj/git-playground","name":"git-playground","description":"A virtual sandbox where beginners can play around with Git and visualize how Git works under the hood.","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":12,"forks":0,"created":"2021-03-04T18:20:47Z","updated":"2021-04-26T15:53:17Z","license":"MIT","branch":"master","homepage":"https://nilaymaj.github.io/git-playground","topics":["git","react"],"demo":"https://nilaymaj.github.io/git-playground","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T19:08:25.295Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-16T19:08:25.295Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-16T19:08:25.295Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T21:05:36.126Z","stars":12,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-16T19:08:25.295Z","stars":12,"forks":0}],"technologies":["React"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A very simple web app to play around with the basic Git commands. Execute commands like add, commit, checkout and reset to see how the file system, object storage and index file change.","This project is only semi-functional. While the basic command usages work, a lot of basic Git functionality (like creating branches) is incomplete. Also, the UI for staging area and commit view is entirely unimplemented.","This idea seemed good before I started the project, but I realized en route that beyond the extreme basic Git commands, such an app loses its utility. Commit-graph dedicated tools like Learn Git Branching perform a much, much better job at teaching Git than this project ever will, if I continued this."],"features":["The Git shim (src/simulator): A basic implementation of the Git internal architecture - object storage, refs,","The web UI (src/app): React frontend for the user."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/nilaymaj/git-playground/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"825e617576c9498faa5e91686dbcbb2cad50f9584a3c46e2dc507385dfc4629b","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T21:05:36.543Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T21:05: